# Local settings for this machine. Copy to local.env; it is not in version
# control.
#
# Both launchers source local.env before working anything out, so settings here
# survive a restart started from the browser. That matters: pressing Restart in
# the web UI makes the app server re-launch the launcher, and anything exported
# only in your shell is gone by then. Choosing the Flash-Next model in the
# browser without this file would start it with the Homebrew llama-server,
# which does not know the qwen3next architecture, and the load would fail.
#
# The ":=" form means the environment still wins, so a one-off
#   LLAMA_SERVER_BIN=... ./scripts/qwen_service.sh restart
# still overrides what is written here.

# A llama.cpp build that knows every architecture you use. The flash-next
# build knows both qwen35 (the 27B) and qwen3next (Flash-Next), so one binary
# serves both and the browser switcher works between them.
: "${LLAMA_SERVER_BIN:=$HOME/local-llm/llama.cpp-flash-next/build/bin/llama-server}"

# Other settings that are worth keeping across restarts, if you want them.
# : "${LLAMA_SERVER_CTX:=32768}"
# : "${REVIEW_PASSES:=3}"
# : "${LLAMA_REASONING_EFFORT:=medium}"
